IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `it-types`

-- Income Tax Act 2007, personal income tax — GOAL 4: SECONDARY TAX CODES.
--
--   "At what flat rate is PAYE withheld from a payment under this tax code?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2007_97.txt — Schedule 2,
-- part A, clauses 1-9.

§ `Goal 4 — tax codes`

-- Schedule 2, part A: "3 ... a non-notified tax code ... 0.45 ... 4 S ...
-- 0.175 ... 5 SH ... 0.300 ... 6 ST ... 0.330 ... 6B SA ... 0.390 ... 7 CAE or
-- EDW ... 0.175 ... 8 NSW ... 0.105 ... 9 SB ... 0.105 for each dollar of the
-- payment." Clauses 1-2: M and ME use the Commissioner's PAYE tables, which
-- are not in the Act.
@ref Schedule 2, part A, cls 1-9
@export The flat rate of PAYE for each dollar of a payment under a tax code, by Schedule 2, part A of the Income Tax Act 2007 (NZ): 0.45 for a non-notified code, 0.175 for S, 0.30 for SH, 0.33 for ST, 0.39 for SA, 0.105 for SB, 0.175 for CAE or EDW, 0.105 for NSW; the M and ME codes use the Commissioner's PAYE tables (refused). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN code IS A `Tax code`  @desc The employee's tax code
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` code MEANS
    CONSIDER code
    WHEN `a non-notified tax code` THEN 0.45
    WHEN `S` THEN 0.175
    WHEN `SH` THEN 0.30
    WHEN `ST` THEN 0.33
    WHEN `SA` THEN 0.39
    WHEN `SB` THEN 0.105
    WHEN `CAE or EDW` THEN 0.175
    WHEN `NSW` THEN 0.105
    WHEN `M or ME` THEN `M and ME codes use the Commissioner's PAYE tables`

`M and ME codes use the Commissioner's PAYE tables` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 2, part A, cls 1-2: the M and ME codes use the Commissioner's PAYE tables, which are not in the Act"

@ref Schedule 2, part A, cls 3-9
GIVEN payment IS A NUMBER, code IS A `Tax code`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the PAYE on a payment of` payment `under tax code` code MEANS
    `the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` code TIMES payment
